From: lane-coordinator <agent@creation-guidelines>
Date: Thu, 19 Nov 2026 05:29:35 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] arm64: dts: qcom: pm6150: Describe the PMIC watchdog

The PON of PM6150 carries the same PMIC watchdog as PM8998. Describe
it, with its bark interrupt, and leave it disabled for boards to enable.

Written with an AI coding assistant (Claude); reviewed and tested as
described in the cover letter.
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm6150.dtsi | 6 ++++++
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm6150.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm6150.dtsi
index 59524609f..2464d3856 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm6150.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/pm6150.dtsi
@@ -61,6 +61,12 @@ pm6150_resin: resin {
 				bias-pull-up;
 				status = "disabled";
 			};
+
+			pm6150_wdt: watchdog {
+				compatible = "qcom,pm6150-wdt", "qcom,pm8998-wdt";
+				interrupts = <0x0 0x8 6 IRQ_TYPE_EDGE_RISING>;
+				status = "disabled";
+			};
 		};
 
 		pm6150_vbus: usb-vbus-regulator@1100 {
-- 
